  "articleBody": "Installing a new showerhead seems straightforward, but it’s easy to make a few common blunders that can lead to leaks or poor performance. One of the biggest mistakes is overtightening. While you want a secure fit, using pipe wrenches or pliers when the manufacturer specifies hand-tightening can strip threads or crack the new fixture. Another common error is neglecting the proper sealing method. Some showerheads need thread seal tape, others rely on rubber washers, and some even combine both. Always follow the manufacturer's instructions to avoid drips. Don't forget to clean the shower arm threads thoroughly before putting on the new head – old tape or residue can create an imperfect seal. For handheld units, people sometimes install hose ends or vacuum-breaker parts in the wrong direction, which can restrict flow or even prevent it entirely. And with adjustable heads, sometimes folks forget to test all the spray settings *before* declaring the job done, missing a potential issue. If you're finding persistent leaks, low water flow, or stripped threads from a previous install, that's a good sign it’s time to call in a remodeling expert like HH Remodeling LLC in the Denver area. We're happy to step in and make sure your shower works just right.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
